    "parent": "util-stats-metrics-plumbing",
    "kind": "meta",
    "title": "Calibrate the per-seed noise floor of depth>=k and h*Rate before spending on coverage-key experiments",
    "description": "Reporting-only probe: run the existing sequential harness on general_vr/VR.spur at 6 seeds (1000-1005) with no code change, and record the per-seed spread of depthAtLeast[4..8], h1/h2/h2b/h3Rate, meanPrefixDepth and runsPerSec. Emit a single observation giving the standard deviation and the minimum detectable effect at the current 2-seed x 54k-run protocol. Touch no spur or scheduler files; harness invocation only.",
    "category": "tooling",
    "buildsOn": [
      "eval harness metrics serialization",
      "sequential fidelity runs"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 4,
    "expectedCost": 1,
    "rationale": "This evaluation showed 2-seed spread (depth>=5 varying by 136 runs, h3Rate by 0.004) that is the same order as several recent accepted objectiveDeltas, meaning auto_merge verdicts on ~1e-4 deltas are currently indistinguishable from seed noise. Knowing the floor tells the ladder how many seeds a real coverage-key effect needs, and retroactively re-grades borderline merges.",
    "generalityArgument": "Measures the variance of the evaluation apparatus itself; no protocol-specific logic, and the same procedure applies to any spec the harness can run.",
